    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a game project that brings the Proto-Indo-European language\u2014the hypothesized common ancestor of English, Latin, Sanskrit, and the world\u2019s largest language family\u2014back to life. The ancient linguistic spirits, said to have existed around 6,000 years ago, are reborn as \u201cWild Words.\u201d<br>Using the etymological learning method, which allows players to associate and memorize words by tracing them back to their roots, the game helps build a rich, three-dimensional vocabulary network in the brain. While this method is highly effective, it has traditionally been difficult and inaccessible to beginners.<br>Our game solves this problem through its unique characters and gameplay systems. Players collect the \u201cancestors\u201d of English words, filling out a bestiary-like compendium and reconstructing a modern dictionary in a brand-new, gamified way.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a game project that brings the Proto-Indo-European language\u2014the hypothesized common ancestor of English, Latin, Sanskrit, and the world\u2019s largest language family\u2014back to life. The ancient linguistic spirits, said to have existed around 6,000 years ago, are reborn as \u201cWild Words.\u201d<br>Using the etymological learning method, which allows players to associate and memorize words by tracing them back to their roots, the game helps build a rich, three-dimensional vocabulary network in the brain. While this method is highly effective, it has traditionally been difficult and inaccessible to beginners.<br>Our game solves this problem through its unique characters and gameplay systems. Players collect the \u201cancestors\u201d of English words, filling out a bestiary-like compendium and reconstructing a modern dictionary in a brand-new, gamified way.</p>",
    "short_description": "Language learning x roguelike. The incarnations of an ancient language (Proto-Indo-European) that is said to have existed about 6,000 years ago are reborn as &quot;Wild Words&quot;!",
